            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0577" n="501" xml:id="pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File 812.00/17582a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to all American Consuls on
                        the Mexican Border except Consul Simpich </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-22T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ascertain and telegraph immediately number and location infantry, cavalry and
                    artillery forces now stationed along border in your district; also number
                    cannon. Have forces in your district been increased since March 10, if so, to
                    what extent? Keep Department promptly informed of proposed and actual changes of
                    these forces.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
